# ---- Sentry reporter for bash lanes (optional, BH-5617) ----
# bin/lib/sentry-report.sh sends one Sentry event when a lane fails in a way
# that used to be only a log line: the autoenqueue ledger skip, the review
# pool capped below 3 by /tmp, and the conductor's WORKER_DEADLINE kill.
# HARNESS_SENTRY_DSN is a SECRET. Set it only in env/global.env (chmod 600).
# It is not a registry knob and has no settings row. Empty or unset = the
# reporter sends nothing and writes nothing.
#HARNESS_SENTRY_DSN=
# Events one fingerprint ([lane, project, reason]) may send in a rolling hour.
# Each attempt counts before the send, so a failing send cannot loop. 0 = off.
# The settings row lib.sentry-report.sentry_max_per_fp_hour wins over this.
#SENTRY_MAX_PER_FP_HOUR=6
